  "body": "Rendering `<video width=500 style=\"border: 1px solid red\">` renders a 500x250 box in all user agents, this means that the following rule apply, from [CSS](https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/visudet.html#inline-replaced-height):\r\n\r\n> Otherwise, if 'height' has a computed value of 'auto', and the element has an intrinsic ratio then the used value of 'height' is:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> (used width) / (intrinsic ratio)\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nBut the HTML spec doesn't specify the default intrinsic ratio of the video element.",
